GT patch 0026: a slow GPU drops pictures instead of slowing the game down.

The end of a frame waited for the GPU to finish the previous one (vkQueueWaitIdle), and the game waited
for the GE thread behind it: with a GPU needing 20-30 ms per frame (an integrated one at a high internal
resolution) the game thread spent 70-90 % of its time blocked, GT's logic and sound (both advance per
frame) ran at 40-75 % speed. Now the pending submit has a fence; a frame that only draws into shown
framebuffers — the two shown last — waits at most 4 ms for it and is otherwise dropped, at most twice in a row (frames that draw elsewhere — a
reflection, an effect reused later — still wait). The software path's present no longer waits for the
queue either. GT_SIM_GPU_MS=N (testing) makes the GPU take N ms per frame.

